  "question": {
    "text": "In the figure shown below, the charge on the left plate of the 10F capacitor is -30C. The charge on the right plate of the 6F capacitor is:\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/ALvPJ3H_PoydhJJjRJpcveCR0UhCBH_n07OPfhm7IHQ.original.fullsize.png\">",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ESRXf",
      "text": "$-12 \\mu \\mathrm{C}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "nmMv8",
      "text": "$+12 \\mu \\mathrm{C}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "YL0ZJ",
      "text": "$-18 \\mu \\mathrm{C}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Ccxsc",
      "text": "$+18 \\mu \\mathrm{C}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/hQlrAEfPQGJRsolRyyhb7HSrTP0RMCpjxI0ajRABDFE.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\nAs given in the figure, $6 \\mu \\mathrm{F}$ and $4 \\mu \\mathrm{F}$ are in parallel. Now using charge conservation\r\n\r\nCharge on $6 \\mu F$ capacitor $=\\frac{6}{6+4} \\times 30=18 \\mu C$\r\n\r\nSince charge is asked on right plate therefore is $+18 \\mu C$",
    "image": null
  },
